The {{nihongo|'''Honda clan'''|本多氏|Honda-shi}} is a Sanese clan who were became an integral political force during the unification period of [[Okaiken]] as well as during the Honda period. Before [[Honda Shigetada]] succeeded in 1600, the Honda clan claimed direct descendant of the Imperial family through [[Emperor Mizuno]]. The early history of the clan and its connections to the imperial family before Shigetada's accession remain a mystery.

When Honda Shigetada, an adopted son of [[Honda Shigenobu]] acceded after the death of the latter, he was approached by the Imperial Family claiming his connections with the imperial lineage. He became regent in 1595 and the clan split into two branches after he was proclaimed emperor. Because of the direct connection of the clan to the Imperial household, it is sometimes regarded as the '''Imperial Family of Okaiken'''. 

Today, its clan members continue to be influential into political dialogue. [[Honda Shigetsuma]], the current head of the clan, is the [[Prime Minister of Okaiken]] since 2021. His father, Honda Tadashige, was the [[Prime Minister of Okaiken]] from 1963 to 1966. 
==History==
===Origins===
The Honda clan claims descent from the ancient Imperial family, specifically through [[Emperor Mizuno]], though definitive records from the early period are scarce due to the destruction of the clan's archives during the [[Taiju War]]. Traditionally, the clan served as minor provincial lords in [[Kazusa Province]] (modern [[Miyagi Prefecture]]), acting as retainers to the powerful [[Soga clan]].

===Sengoku Period and the Rise to Power===
The clan's fortunes changed dramatically under the leadership of [[Emperor Shirakawa of Mitoyagi|Honda Shigetada]] (1556–1625). Originally born as '''Prince Fumihito''', the eldest son of [[Emperor Komei of Mitoyagi|Emperor Komei]], he was abducted as a child during the [[Yuzawa Incident]] and raised as a warrior, unaware of his heritage. Adopted by the Honda clan leader [[Honda Shigenobu]] (later corrected to Shigetatsu in some records), Shigetada became a fearsome general known as the "Warrior who surpassed Death."

Following the assassination of the warlord [[Ogasawara Terumasa]] and the subsequent power vacuum, Shigetada unified the nation at the [[Battle of Tone]] in 1600. In 1610, his true lineage was revealed, and he ascended the throne as '''Emperor Shirakawa'''.

===The Great Divergence (1610–1870)===
To ensure stability, Emperor Shirakawa enacted the ''Edict of the Two Realms'', splitting the family into two distinct lines:
* '''The Imperial Line:''' Descended from his eldest son, [[Emperor Daigo of Mitoyagi|Prince Takahito]] (Emperor Daigo), who held spiritual and ceremonial authority.
* '''The Shogunal Line (Okami Branch):''' Descended from his second son, [[Honda Shigetomo]], who held military and administrative authority as the [[Honda Shoguns]].

This system of "Dual Sovereignty" ruled [[Okaiken]] for over 250 years. The Shogunal line faced several succession crises. The direct line of Shigetomo ended with the 9th Shogun, [[Honda Shigenari]]. The title then passed to the **Yamanaka Branch** (descendants of a younger brother of the 8th Shogun), and finally to the **Fujisato Branch** (descendants of the 3rd son, [[Honda Shigetoki]]) in the mid-19th century with the adoption of [[Honda Yoshinobu]].

===Modern Era (1870–Present)===
Following the [[Saito Restoration]] in 1870, the last Shogun, '''Honda Yoshinobu''', voluntarily returned administrative power to his cousin, [[Saito of Mitoyagi|Emperor Saito]]. The Shogunate was abolished, and the Honda family was incorporated into the ''Kazoku'' peerage system, with Yoshinobu receiving the title of Prince (''Kōshaku'').

While the Imperial line remained the heads of state, the former Shogunal family transitioned seamlessly into modern politics. Yoshinobu's grandson, [[Honda Tadashige]], served as the [[Prime Minister of Okaiken]] from 1963 to 1966, overseeing the "Sanese Economic Miracle." His brother, [[Honda Shigehara]], also served as Prime Minister (1990–1993) during the establishment of the current coalition system.

Today, the clan is led by [[Honda Shigetsuma]], a dominant figure in the [[Progressive Party of Okaiken]], continuing the family's legacy of governance.

